<title>USA: GM has 10,297 U.S. workers idled by strike.</title>
<headline>GM has 10,297 U.S. workers idled by strike.</headline>
<dateline>WARREN, Mich. 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Motors Corp said as of 1100 EDT there were 10,297 GM North American employees laid off as a result of the Canadian Auto Workers strike that began October 3.</p>
<p>In addition to layoffs at its vehicle and powertrain assembly plants, there were 6,046 workers idled at its Delphi Automotive Systems parts and components division, which is based in Pontiac, Mich.</p>
<p>-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
